<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dong Chang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 896</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dong Chang (died 896) was a late Tang warlord who controlled Yuezhou, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhejiang">Zhejiang</a>, as military governor. In 895 he proclaimed himself emperor of a state called Luoping, but the Tang court ordered his former subordinate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qian-liu">Qian Liu</a> to suppress him, and Qian Liu's forces captured him in 896. His defeat gave Qian Liu control of the Zhejiang region, the basis of the later Wuyue kingdom.</p></div>
